{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AsELJ7WT8UvzLJY3pZehFQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 2 output, approved 2026-06-11. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`\n4\t> (this folder). Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Each wave ends GREEN on\n5\t> the ground-truth gate and adds/extends tests under `tests/`.\n6\t\n7\ttest-command: python -m pytest -v\n8\t\n9\t## Conventions (read before any wave)\n10\t\n11\t- **Active Anchor project id:** read it from `rnd_registry.json` at build time\n12\t  (the live \"Anchor\" project; do not hard-code â€” it may differ).\n13\t- **No live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the gate.** Model interactions go\n14\t  through `tests/fake_claude.py` via `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`; PTY interactions go\n15\t  through a **stub PTY backend** selected by an env override (e.g.\n16\t  `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`) that runs a fake pty-able child. Real `pywinpty` is\n17\t  used only at runtime, never in pytest.\n18\t- **pywinpty is the ONLY permitted native dependency, isolated to the terminal\n19\t  subsystem.** Import it lazily; if the import fails, the terminal subsystem\n20\t  reports \"real terminal unavailable\" and the rest of Anchor is unaffected. Add\n21\t  it to the dev/runtime extras, NOT to the stdlib-only core import path.\n22\t- **f-string discipline** in `anchor_gui.py`: double literal braces in generated\n23\t  CSS/JS; `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` stays a RAW single-brace string.\n24\t- **Security:** every new mutating / terminal / preview-run / worktree endpoint\n25\t  sits behind the existing `do_POST` token-auth gate. GET stays read-only.\n26\t- **Mirror** new backend data functions into `anchor.py` where natural (Wave 9\n27\t  sweeps the rest).\n28\t- Reuse, don't fork: build on v2's `sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`,\n29\t  `rnd_terminal.py`, `deliverables.py`, `job_runner.py`, `report_viewer.py`,\n30\t  `vendor/xterm`.\n31\t\n32\t## Wave 1 â€” ConPTY-under-service spike (GATES THE WHOLE BUILD)\n33\t\n34\tProve a real ConPTY terminal can run under the non-interactive `anchor` service\n35\t(session 0) before building the session manager on top of it. Create\n36\t`pty_manager.py` with a **backend seam**: a `pywinpty` backend and a `stub`\n37\tbackend (env-selected). Implement the minimal manager core: `start(cmd, cwd, env)\n38\t-> session_id`, `write(session_id, bytes)`, `read_since(session_id, cursor)`,\n39\t`resize(session_id, cols, rows)`, `kill(session_id)`. Unit-test the manager logic\n40\tagainst the **stub** backend. SEPARATELY, provide a runnable spike\n41\t(`spike_conpty_service.py` or a documented orchestrator step) that launches a real\n42\tinteractive child (e.g. `cmd`/`claude`) via pywinpty under a faithfully simulated\n43\tservice context (no loaded profile; `USERPROFILE`/`HOME`=`C:\\Users\\john`; full\n44\tsystem env minus profile vars â€” per the runtime memory pitfall) and confirms\n45\tbidirectional bytes.\n46\t\n47\t- **Done-when:** (a) `pytest` is GREEN with the stub-backend manager tests; AND\n48\t  (b) the empirical spike demonstrates a real pywinpty child running + echoing\n49\t  bytes under the simulated service context, recorded in EXECUTION-LOG.\n50\t- **HALT condition (per user gate):** if the empirical ConPTY-under-service spike\n51\t  FAILS, Foreman HALTS and surfaces the fallback options (john-owned session\n52\t  broker; or REPL revert) to the user â€” it does NOT silently proceed or downgrade.\n53\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the stub PTY backend, **When** the manager starts a child,\n54\t  writes input, and reads output, **Then** the echoed bytes round-trip and\n55\t  `kill` reaps the child; **and** the empirical spike log shows a real pywinpty\n56\t  child streaming under the simulated service env.\n57\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_pty_manager.py` (stub backend: start/write/read/resize/\n58\t  kill, unknown-session errors, reap-on-kill).\n59\t\n60\t## Wave 2 â€” Durable session registry + git-worktree isolation\n61\t\n62\tNew `session_registry.py` (persisted under `.anchor/`, survives restart) modeling\n63\ta managed session: `{session_id, project_id, lane, backend(claude|gemini),\n64\tworktree_path, branch, status, created_at, label}`. New `worktrees.py`:\n65\t`create_worktree(project_id, session_id) -> (path, branch)` (git worktree+branch\n66\tunder a managed, git-ignored location OUTSIDE the tracked tree),\n67\t`remove_worktree(session_id)` (with safety checks), and a `reap_orphans()` sweep.\n68\tWire registry persistence + recovery (reconcile registry vs live processes/worktrees\n69\ton load). No UI yet.\n70\t\n71\t- **Done-when:** a session can be registered with its own worktree+branch; two\n72\t  concurrent sessions get independent worktrees that don't share a working tree;\n73\t  removing a session removes its worktree; `reap_orphans` cleans a worktree whose\n74\t  session is gone; the registry round-trips across a simulated restart.\n75\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** an active Anchor git repo, **When** two sessions are\n76\t  created, **Then** each has a distinct worktree path + branch and a dirty file in\n77\t  one is invisible to the other; **When** one is killed, **Then** its worktree is\n78\t  removed and the other is untouched.\n79\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_session_registry.py`, `tests/test_worktrees.py`\n80\t  (hermetic: a temp git repo; create/isolate/remove/reap/recover).\n81\t\n82\t## Wave 3 â€” ConPTY terminal manager + transport + auth\n83\t\n84\tTie Wave-1 `pty_manager` + Wave-2 registry/worktrees into the live session\n85\tservice: `start_session(project_id, lane, backend)` creates a worktree, launches a\n86\t**bare interactive** `claude`/`gemini` PTY in it (NO auto-seeded skill), registers\n87\tit; `attach`/`detach`/`input`/`resize`/`kill`. Add the browser transport: a\n88\tminimal **stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket** endpoint (`/api/rnd/term_ws`) carrying\n89\tPTY bytes both ways, with an **SSE-out + POST-in fallback** (`/api/rnd/term_stream2`\n90\t+ `/api/rnd/term_input2`). All terminal endpoints are **token-authed**. Reattach\n91\treplays the live screen buffer.\n92\t\n93\t- **Done-when:** startâ†’attachâ†’typeâ†’see-outputâ†’detach (process keeps running)â†’\n94\t  reattach (buffer replays)â†’kill works against the stub backend over the chosen\n95\t  transport; endpoints reject unauthenticated requests.\n96\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a started stub session, **When** the client detaches and\n97\t  reattaches, **Then** the session is still running and prior output replays;\n98\t  **When** an unauthenticated request hits a terminal endpoint, **Then** it is 401.\n99\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_terminal_session.py` (start/attach/detach/reattach/kill,\n100\t  buffer replay, auth, WS-frame or SSE framing well-formed without hanging).\n101\t\n102\t## Wave 4 â€” Stacking window-manager UI\n103\t\n104\tFront-end in `anchor_gui` (dashboard + `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`): a top bar of terse\n105\t**status-colored session buttons** (\"plan 1\", \"research 2\", \"foreman 1\");\n106\tclicking opens/attaches an xterm.js terminal **window**; windows **stack like\n107\tbricks**, are draggable/resizable/minimizable; minimize keeps the session\n108\trunning; **X = kill with an \"Are you sure?\" confirm**. Status colors per the\n109\tlocked mapping (green=working, amber=needs-you/done, red=failed, grey=idle),\n110\tdriven by session status. On dashboard load, repopulate buttons/windows from the\n111\tregistry.\n112\t\n113\t- **Done-when:** the served HTML/JS includes the session-button bar, the\n114\t  stacking/minimizable window container wired to the Wave-3 endpoints, the\n115\t  kill-confirm dialog, and the status-color classes; reopening reflects live\n116\t  sessions. (Behavioral terminal feel verified in-browser, out of gate scope.)\n117\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** â‰¥2 live sessions, **When** the dashboard renders, **Then**\n118\t  two status-colored buttons appear and the window manager can open/stack/minimize\n119\t  them; **When** X is clicked, **Then** a confirm dialog gates the kill.\n120\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_project_window.py` / `tests/test_rnd_ui_wiring.py`\n121\t  (button bar markup, status-color classes, kill-confirm wiring, brace hygiene,\n122\t  repopulate-from-registry hook).\n123\t\n124\t## Wave 5 â€” Thin project rows + accurate proactive project summary\n125\t\n126\tReplace the square tile with a thin full-width row (name Â· summary Â· per-lane\n127\tmini-counts Â· status dot; clickâ†’window; lifecycle controls in a kebab/hover\n128\tmenu). Add a background **project-summary** generator (extend `summarizer.py`):\n129\tgenerate ONCE from CLAUDE.md + recent plan docs + deliverables, cached,\n130\tregenerable; replaces the weak blurb. Generation runs proactively (on rescan)\n131\tthrough the runner seam.\n132\t\n133\t- **Done-when:** the main dashboard renders thin full-width rows; the Anchor row\n134\t  shows an accurate cached project summary (not the old first-paragraph blurb);\n135\t  lifecycle controls still reachable from the kebab; row click opens the window.\n136\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the Anchor project, **When** the dashboard renders, **Then**\n137\t  it is a one-line full-width row with a cached accurate summary and a working\n138\t  click-to-open; **Then** no wasted right-half square remains.\n139\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_tile_render.py` (thin-row markup, cached project\n140\t  summary present, kebab controls), `tests/test_summarizer.py` (project-summary\n141\t  generate-once + cache).\n142\t\n143\t## Wave 6 â€” In-place expandable session summaries (content fix + links + effort)\n144\t\n145\tMake clicking a session tile EXPAND an accordion inline (no `/summary` page).\n146\tImprove summary CONTENT to the locked shape: when-run, what-was-asked, North-Star,\n147\tdocument links (open rendered markdown in a new tab via `report_viewer`), and\n148\teffort (tokens + wall-clock from `job_runner` cost records; imported â†’ \"no run\n149\tmetrics\"). Generate proactively (Wave-5 mechanism) + cache; lazy \"generatingâ€¦\"\n150\tonly as fallback. Add a \"Launch new session\" button inside the expanded panel\n151\tthat calls Wave-3 `start_session` seeded from this session.\n152\t\n153\t- **Done-when:** clicking the brownfield-discovery planning session expands an\n154\t  inline panel with the accurate cached summary + working doc links + effort +\n155\t  a \"Launch new session\" button; collapses back; no navigation to a separate\n156\t  page; reopening serves the cache.\n157\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a session with cached summary, **When** its tile is\n158\t  clicked, **Then** an inline accordion shows when/what/North-Star/doc-links/\n159\t  effort and a Launch-new-session control â€” with zero separate-page navigation.\n160\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_project_window.py` (inline-expand markup, doc\n161\t  links, effort rendering, launch-from-panel wiring), `tests/test_summarizer.py`\n162\t  (the richer content fields).\n163\t\n164\t## Wave 7 â€” Stage handoffs\n165\t\n166\tWhen launching a build/execution session, discover the most-recent plan set (from\n167\tthe `.anchor` store / sessions) and present \"execute on this plan set?\" â€”\n168\tpre-staging the worktree and surfacing the plan doc paths. Record handoff context\n169\tin the per-project Anchor reference (`Anchor.md`/`discovery.json`). General lane\n170\t\"Launch new session\" seeds prior-stage outputs.\n171\t\n172\t- **Done-when:** launching a build session for Anchor proposes the most-recent\n173\t  rnd-v* plan set and, on confirm, stages a worktree primed with those plan paths.\n174\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** existing planning sessions, **When** a build session is\n175\t  launched, **Then** the most-recent plan set is offered and confirming primes the\n176\t  session worktree with those docs referenced.\n177\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_handoff.py` (most-recent-plan discovery, confirmâ†’prime,\n178\t  Anchor.md handoff record).\n179\t\n180\t## Wave 8 â€” Runnable Anchor deliverable (ephemeral preview)\n181\t\n182\tPin `anchor_gui.py` as the Anchor deliverable (extend `deliverables.py`). Add a\n183\t**Run** action: spin up a preview `anchor_gui.py` on an **OS-assigned ephemeral\n184\tport** in a worktree/copy (NEVER binding 8777 / never touching the live service),\n185\tregister it as a preview session, open it, and reap it on stop. Auth-gated.\n186\t\n187\t- **Done-when:** the Anchor project shows `anchor_gui.py` as a deliverable; the\n188\t  Run action launches a preview instance on a free port (â‰ 8777), returns its URL,\n189\t  and the preview can be stopped/reaped; the live service is untouched.\n190\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the pinned deliverable, **When** Run is clicked, **Then** a\n191\t  preview server starts on an ephemeral port and is reachable, and Stop reaps it;\n192\t  **Then** 8777 / the live service is never bound or disturbed.\n193\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_deliverable_run.py` (ephemeral-port preview start/stop/\n194\t  reap, never-8777 assertion, auth).\n195\t\n196\t## Wave 9 â€” Ghost World Labs branding on the Home page\n197\t\n198\tBrand the Anchor home page as a **Ghost World Labs** tool, **powered by NextGen\n199\tNuclear**, in a stylish way that fits the existing dark theme. Vendor the brand\n200\tmark from `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\GWL-M-Icon.svg` (a ghost on dark slate `#0f172a`\n201\twith a green glow `#22c55e` and a â˜¢ radioactive symbol â€” note: â˜¢ already encodes\n202\tthe NextGen Nuclear tie-in; palette matches Anchor's theme) into Anchor's static\n203\tassets (e.g. `vendor/brand/gwl-m-icon.svg`) served via a traversal-safe static\n204\troute, and also set it as the dashboard `favicon`. Add a tasteful home-page\n205\theader/footer treatment: the ghost mark + a **\"Ghost World Labs\"** wordmark + a\n206\tsmall **\"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"** badge, using the brand palette\n207\t(`#0f172a` / `#22c55e` / `#f8fafc`). Keep it elegant and unobtrusive (a header\n208\tlockup and/or a footer credit), not garish. f-string brace discipline applies.\n209\t\n210\t- **Done-when:** the served home-page HTML includes the GWL mark asset, the\n211\t  \"Ghost World Labs\" wordmark, and a \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear\" badge, styled to\n212\t  match the theme; the favicon is the GWL mark; the brand asset is served by a\n213\t  path-traversal-safe static route.\n214\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the dashboard, **When** the home page renders, **Then** it\n215\t  shows the Ghost World Labs lockup + the NextGen Nuclear credit + the GWL favicon,\n216\t  and the `/vendor/brand/` route serves the SVG and blocks `../` traversal.\n217\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_tile_render.py` or add `tests/test_branding.py`\n218\t  (home-page lockup markup, favicon wired, brand static route serves + traversal-\n219\t  safe).\n220\t\n221\t## Wave 10 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro-scan/docs\n222\t\n223\tMirror new backend data functions into `anchor.py` (sessions/registry/handoff/\n224\tdeliverable-run inspection where sensible). Extend `anchor_healthcheck.py` to walk\n225\tthe v3 surface (session registry, stub-PTY session lifecycle, proactive summary,\n226\tdeliverable-run preview) â€” fully stubbed. Update the **distribution scan** to\n227\tallow the declared `pywinpty` terminal-subsystem exception (and confirm it still\n228\trefuses other native/secret leakage). Update `CLAUDE.md`.\n229\t\n230\t- **Done-when:** `python anchor_healthcheck.py` (or its suite equivalent) walks\n231\t  the v3 surface clean and stubbed; the distro scan passes with the declared\n232\t  pywinpty exception; full `python -m pytest -v` is GREEN; `CLAUDE.md` documents v3.\n233\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_distro_scan.py` (pywinpty exception declared, no\n234\t  other leakage), `tests/test_healthcheck_*`; suite green overall.\n235\t\n236\t## Project DONE\n237\t\n238\tAll ten waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`; the dashboard shows thin\n239\tfull-width project rows with accurate cached summaries; session tiles expand\n240\tin-place with accurate summaries + doc links + effort; trio work runs as\n241\tpersistent, worktree-isolated, status-colored ConPTY terminal sessions managed as\n242\tstacking windows that survive disconnect; stage handoffs work; the home page is\n243\tbranded as a Ghost World Labs tool powered by NextGen Nuclear; and the Anchor\n244\tdeliverable runs as an ephemeral preview. Wave 10 is the terminal/closing wave.\n245\t**Note:** Wave 1's ConPTY-under-service empirical proof is a HARD GATE â€” a failure\n246\tthere HALTS to the user before any further wave proceeds.\n247\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8a086ba-f793-4585-9aab-75cfcc33428a","uuid":"6547d07e-2f0c-4ef1-8032-ca62191ea7d2","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:19:04.162Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v3\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\n> Crucible Stage 2 output, approved 2026-06-11. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`\n> (this folder). Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Each wave ends GREEN on\n> the ground-truth gate and adds/extends tests under `tests/`.\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest -v\n\n## Conventions (read before any wave)\n\n- **Active Anchor project id:** read it from `rnd_registry.json` at build time\n  (the live \"Anchor\" project; do not hard-code â€” it may differ).\n- **No live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the gate.** Model interactions go\n  through `tests/fake_claude.py` via `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`; PTY interactions go\n  through a **stub PTY backend** selected by an env override (e.g.\n  `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`) that runs a fake pty-able child. Real `pywinpty` is\n  used only at runtime, never in pytest.\n- **pywinpty is the ONLY permitted native dependency, isolated to the terminal\n  subsystem.** Import it lazily; if the import fails, the terminal subsystem\n  reports \"real terminal unavailable\" and the rest of Anchor is unaffected. Add\n  it to the dev/runtime extras, NOT to the stdlib-only core import path.\n- **f-string discipline** in `anchor_gui.py`: double literal braces in generated\n  CSS/JS; `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` stays a RAW single-brace string.\n- **Security:** every new mutating / terminal / preview-run / worktree endpoint\n  sits behind the existing `do_POST` token-auth gate. GET stays read-only.\n- **Mirror** new backend data functions into `anchor.py` where natural (Wave 9\n  sweeps the rest).\n- Reuse, don't fork: build on v2's `sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`,\n  `rnd_terminal.py`, `deliverables.py`, `job_runner.py`, `report_viewer.py`,\n  `vendor/xterm`.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” ConPTY-under-service spike (GATES THE WHOLE BUILD)\n\nProve a real ConPTY terminal can run under the non-interactive `anchor` service\n(session 0) before building the session manager on top of it. Create\n`pty_manager.py` with a **backend seam**: a `pywinpty` backend and a `stub`\nbackend (env-selected). Implement the minimal manager core: `start(cmd, cwd, env)\n-> session_id`, `write(session_id, bytes)`, `read_since(session_id, cursor)`,\n`resize(session_id, cols, rows)`, `kill(session_id)`. Unit-test the manager logic\nagainst the **stub** backend. SEPARATELY, provide a runnable spike\n(`spike_conpty_service.py` or a documented orchestrator step) that launches a real\ninteractive child (e.g. `cmd`/`claude`) via pywinpty under a faithfully simulated\nservice context (no loaded profile; `USERPROFILE`/`HOME`=`C:\\Users\\john`; full\nsystem env minus profile vars â€” per the runtime memory pitfall) and confirms\nbidirectional bytes.\n\n- **Done-when:** (a) `pytest` is GREEN with the stub-backend manager tests; AND\n  (b) the empirical spike demonstrates a real pywinpty child running + echoing\n  bytes under the simulated service context, recorded in EXECUTION-LOG.\n- **HALT condition (per user gate):** if the empirical ConPTY-under-service spike\n  FAILS, Foreman HALTS and surfaces the fallback options (john-owned session\n  broker; or REPL revert) to the user â€” it does NOT silently proceed or downgrade.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the stub PTY backend, **When** the manager starts a child,\n  writes input, and reads output, **Then** the echoed bytes round-trip and\n  `kill` reaps the child; **and** the empirical spike log shows a real pywinpty\n  child streaming under the simulated service env.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_pty_manager.py` (stub backend: start/write/read/resize/\n  kill, unknown-session errors, reap-on-kill).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Durable session registry + git-worktree isolation\n\nNew `session_registry.py` (persisted under `.anchor/`, survives restart) modeling\na managed session: `{session_id, project_id, lane, backend(claude|gemini),\nworktree_path, branch, status, created_at, label}`. New `worktrees.py`:\n`create_worktree(project_id, session_id) -> (path, branch)` (git worktree+branch\nunder a managed, git-ignored location OUTSIDE the tracked tree),\n`remove_worktree(session_id)` (with safety checks), and a `reap_orphans()` sweep.\nWire registry persistence + recovery (reconcile registry vs live processes/worktrees\non load). No UI yet.\n\n- **Done-when:** a session can be registered with its own worktree+branch; two\n  concurrent sessions get independent worktrees that don't share a working tree;\n  removing a session removes its worktree; `reap_orphans` cleans a worktree whose\n  session is gone; the registry round-trips across a simulated restart.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** an active Anchor git repo, **When** two sessions are\n  created, **Then** each has a distinct worktree path + branch and a dirty file in\n  one is invisible to the other; **When** one is killed, **Then** its worktree is\n  removed and the other is untouched.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_session_registry.py`, `tests/test_worktrees.py`\n  (hermetic: a temp git repo; create/isolate/remove/reap/recover).\n\n## Wave 3 â€” ConPTY terminal manager + transport + auth\n\nTie Wave-1 `pty_manager` + Wave-2 registry/worktrees into the live session\nservice: `start_session(project_id, lane, backend)` creates a worktree, launches a\n**bare interactive** `claude`/`gemini` PTY in it (NO auto-seeded skill), registers\nit; `attach`/`detach`/`input`/`resize`/`kill`. Add the browser transport: a\nminimal **stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket** endpoint (`/api/rnd/term_ws`) carrying\nPTY bytes both ways, with an **SSE-out + POST-in fallback** (`/api/rnd/term_stream2`\n+ `/api/rnd/term_input2`). All terminal endpoints are **token-authed**. Reattach\nreplays the live screen buffer.\n\n- **Done-when:** startâ†’attachâ†’typeâ†’see-outputâ†’detach (process keeps running)â†’\n  reattach (buffer replays)â†’kill works against the stub backend over the chosen\n  transport; endpoints reject unauthenticated requests.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a started stub session, **When** the client detaches and\n  reattaches, **Then** the session is still running and prior output replays;\n  **When** an unauthenticated request hits a terminal endpoint, **Then** it is 401.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_terminal_session.py` (start/attach/detach/reattach/kill,\n  buffer replay, auth, WS-frame or SSE framing well-formed without hanging).\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Stacking window-manager UI\n\nFront-end in `anchor_gui` (dashboard + `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`): a top bar of terse\n**status-colored session buttons** (\"plan 1\", \"research 2\", \"foreman 1\");\nclicking opens/attaches an xterm.js terminal **window**; windows **stack like\nbricks**, are draggable/resizable/minimizable; minimize keeps the session\nrunning; **X = kill with an \"Are you sure?\" confirm**. Status colors per the\nlocked mapping (green=working, amber=needs-you/done, red=failed, grey=idle),\ndriven by session status. On dashboard load, repopulate buttons/windows from the\nregistry.\n\n- **Done-when:** the served HTML/JS includes the session-button bar, the\n  stacking/minimizable window container wired to the Wave-3 endpoints, the\n  kill-confirm dialog, and the status-color classes; reopening reflects live\n  sessions. (Behavioral terminal feel verified in-browser, out of gate scope.)\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** â‰¥2 live sessions, **When** the dashboard renders, **Then**\n  two status-colored buttons appear and the window manager can open/stack/minimize\n  them; **When** X is clicked, **Then** a confirm dialog gates the kill.\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_project_window.py` / `tests/test_rnd_ui_wiring.py`\n  (button bar markup, status-color classes, kill-confirm wiring, brace hygiene,\n  repopulate-from-registry hook).\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Thin project rows + accurate proactive project summary\n\nReplace the square tile with a thin full-width row (name Â· summary Â· per-lane\nmini-counts Â· status dot; clickâ†’window; lifecycle controls in a kebab/hover\nmenu). Add a background **project-summary** generator (extend `summarizer.py`):\ngenerate ONCE from CLAUDE.md + recent plan docs + deliverables, cached,\nregenerable; replaces the weak blurb. Generation runs proactively (on rescan)\nthrough the runner seam.\n\n- **Done-when:** the main dashboard renders thin full-width rows; the Anchor row\n  shows an accurate cached project summary (not the old first-paragraph blurb);\n  lifecycle controls still reachable from the kebab; row click opens the window.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the Anchor project, **When** the dashboard renders, **Then**\n  it is a one-line full-width row with a cached accurate summary and a working\n  click-to-open; **Then** no wasted right-half square remains.\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_tile_render.py` (thin-row markup, cached project\n  summary present, kebab controls), `tests/test_summarizer.py` (project-summary\n  generate-once + cache).\n\n## Wave 6 â€” In-place expandable session summaries (content fix + links + effort)\n\nMake clicking a session tile EXPAND an accordion inline (no `/summary` page).\nImprove summary CONTENT to the locked shape: when-run, what-was-asked, North-Star,\ndocument links (open rendered markdown in a new tab via `report_viewer`), and\neffort (tokens + wall-clock from `job_runner` cost records; imported â†’ \"no run\nmetrics\"). Generate proactively (Wave-5 mechanism) + cache; lazy \"generatingâ€¦\"\nonly as fallback. Add a \"Launch new session\" button inside the expanded panel\nthat calls Wave-3 `start_session` seeded from this session.\n\n- **Done-when:** clicking the brownfield-discovery planning session expands an\n  inline panel with the accurate cached summary + working doc links + effort +\n  a \"Launch new session\" button; collapses back; no navigation to a separate\n  page; reopening serves the cache.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a session with cached summary, **When** its tile is\n  clicked, **Then** an inline accordion shows when/what/North-Star/doc-links/\n  effort and a Launch-new-session control â€” with zero separate-page navigation.\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_project_window.py` (inline-expand markup, doc\n  links, effort rendering, launch-from-panel wiring), `tests/test_summarizer.py`\n  (the richer content fields).\n\n## Wave 7 â€” Stage handoffs\n\nWhen launching a build/execution session, discover the most-recent plan set (from\nthe `.anchor` store / sessions) and present \"execute on this plan set?\" â€”\npre-staging the worktree and surfacing the plan doc paths. Record handoff context\nin the per-project Anchor reference (`Anchor.md`/`discovery.json`). General lane\n\"Launch new session\" seeds prior-stage outputs.\n\n- **Done-when:** launching a build session for Anchor proposes the most-recent\n  rnd-v* plan set and, on confirm, stages a worktree primed with those plan paths.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** existing planning sessions, **When** a build session is\n  launched, **Then** the most-recent plan set is offered and confirming primes the\n  session worktree with those docs referenced.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_handoff.py` (most-recent-plan discovery, confirmâ†’prime,\n  Anchor.md handoff record).\n\n## Wave 8 â€” Runnable Anchor deliverable (ephemeral preview)\n\nPin `anchor_gui.py` as the Anchor deliverable (extend `deliverables.py`). Add a\n**Run** action: spin up a preview `anchor_gui.py` on an **OS-assigned ephemeral\nport** in a worktree/copy (NEVER binding 8777 / never touching the live service),\nregister it as a preview session, open it, and reap it on stop. Auth-gated.\n\n- **Done-when:** the Anchor project shows `anchor_gui.py` as a deliverable; the\n  Run action launches a preview instance on a free port (â‰ 8777), returns its URL,\n  and the preview can be stopped/reaped; the live service is untouched.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the pinned deliverable, **When** Run is clicked, **Then** a\n  preview server starts on an ephemeral port and is reachable, and Stop reaps it;\n  **Then** 8777 / the live service is never bound or disturbed.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_deliverable_run.py` (ephemeral-port preview start/stop/\n  reap, never-8777 assertion, auth).\n\n## Wave 9 â€” Ghost World Labs branding on the Home page\n\nBrand the Anchor home page as a **Ghost World Labs** tool, **powered by NextGen\nNuclear**, in a stylish way that fits the existing dark theme. Vendor the brand\nmark from `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\GWL-M-Icon.svg` (a ghost on dark slate `#0f172a`\nwith a green glow `#22c55e` and a â˜¢ radioactive symbol â€” note: â˜¢ already encodes\nthe NextGen Nuclear tie-in; palette matches Anchor's theme) into Anchor's static\nassets (e.g. `vendor/brand/gwl-m-icon.svg`) served via a traversal-safe static\nroute, and also set it as the dashboard `favicon`. Add a tasteful home-page\nheader/footer treatment: the ghost mark + a **\"Ghost World Labs\"** wordmark + a\nsmall **\"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"** badge, using the brand palette\n(`#0f172a` / `#22c55e` / `#f8fafc`). Keep it elegant and unobtrusive (a header\nlockup and/or a footer credit), not garish. f-string brace discipline applies.\n\n- **Done-when:** the served home-page HTML includes the GWL mark asset, the\n  \"Ghost World Labs\" wordmark, and a \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear\" badge, styled to\n  match the theme; the favicon is the GWL mark; the brand asset is served by a\n  path-traversal-safe static route.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the dashboard, **When** the home page renders, **Then** it\n  shows the Ghost World Labs lockup + the NextGen Nuclear credit + the GWL favicon,\n  and the `/vendor/brand/` route serves the SVG and blocks `../` traversal.\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_tile_render.py` or add `tests/test_branding.py`\n  (home-page lockup markup, favicon wired, brand static route serves + traversal-\n  safe).\n\n## Wave 10 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro-scan/docs\n\nMirror new backend data functions into `anchor.py` (sessions/registry/handoff/\ndeliverable-run inspection where sensible). Extend `anchor_healthcheck.py` to walk\nthe v3 surface (session registry, stub-PTY session lifecycle, proactive summary,\ndeliverable-run preview) â€” fully stubbed. Update the **distribution scan** to\nallow the declared `pywinpty` terminal-subsystem exception (and confirm it still\nrefuses other native/secret leakage). Update `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n- **Done-when:** `python anchor_healthcheck.py` (or its suite equivalent) walks\n  the v3 surface clean and stubbed; the distro scan passes with the declared\n  pywinpty exception; full `python -m pytest -v` is GREEN; `CLAUDE.md` documents v3.\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_distro_scan.py` (pywinpty exception declared, no\n  other leakage), `tests/test_healthcheck_*`; suite green overall.\n\n## Project DONE\n\nAll ten waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`; the dashboard shows thin\nfull-width project rows with accurate cached summaries; session tiles expand\nin-place with accurate summaries + doc links + effort; trio work runs as\npersistent, worktree-isolated, status-colored ConPTY terminal sessions managed as\nstacking windows that survive disconnect; stage handoffs work; the home page is\nbranded as a Ghost World Labs tool powered by NextGen Nuclear; and the Anchor\ndeliverable runs as an ephemeral preview. Wave 10 is the terminal/closing wave.\n**Note:** Wave 1's ConPTY-under-service empirical proof is a HARD GATE â€” a failure\nthere HALTS to the user before any further wave proceeds.\n","numLines":247,"startLine":1,"totalLines":247}}}
