{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KF3iVZXabVFs7n4igybZzv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Planning Session Summary\n\n**Goal / North Star (locked)**\n- Turn the Anchor dashboard into a **durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D**: every project becomes a thin, full-width row with an accurate, auto-generated summary.\n- Clicking any session expands a **cached, in-place** accordion summary (when Â· what-was-asked Â· North-Star Â· clickable doc links Â· effort in tokens+time) â€” never a separate \"no summary\" page.\n- Trio work runs as **persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows (open / attach / minimize / kill-with-confirm), status-colored, surviving disconnect, and feeling like a real Claude/Gemini terminal.\n\n**Locked user-gate decisions (Stage 0/1)**\n- **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY via `pywinpty`** â€” a conscious waiver of Anchor's stdlib-only rule *for the terminal subsystem only*; everything else stays stdlib, and the subsystem degrades gracefully if `pywinpty` is absent.\n- **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached** (generated once at discovery/rescan and right after a run); lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as fallback.\n- **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session** â€” each plan/research/build session gets its own worktree+branch so trees never collide.\n- **Scope = one comprehensive plan** (all of v3 in a single Foreman build).\n- **Wave-1 ConPTY-under-service spike is a HARD GATE** â€” if the empirical spike fails, Foreman HALTS to the user (no silent downgrade).\n- **Status colors:** green = working (ignore) Â· amber = needs-you/done Â· red = failed Â· grey = idle.\n\n**Problem this fixes (verified ground truth, 2026-06-11)**\n- The `anchor` service runs as `.\\john` with working Claude subscription creds, so \"no summary\" was a **UX/architecture issue, not a creds issue**.\n- v2 summaries were generated lazily on click into a separate `/summary` page that rendered empty/failed states (the \"hit summary â†’ no summary\" symptom).\n- The v2 terminal was a stream-json REPL that auto-seeded the lane skill and had a fragile gate-answer path â€” not a faithful terminal; tiles were small squares wasting half each row; Anchor's own `anchor_gui.py` deliverable wasn't represented.\n\n**Frozen architecture (Master Plan, sections Aâ€“I)**\n- (A) Thin full-width project rows; (B) accurate, proactive, cached project + session summaries from `job_runner` cost records; (C) in-place expandable session summaries; (D) durable session registry + ConPTY terminal manager (`pty_manager.py` with a stub backend seam), token-authed WebSocket transport (SSE+POST fallback) into vendored xterm.js; (E) stacking window-manager UI; (F) git-worktree concurrency isolation with an orphan reaper; (G) stage handoffs (build session finds the most-recent plan set); (H) runnable Anchor deliverable as an ephemeral-port preview (never 8777); (I) persistence/robustness under the service.\n\n**Implementation plan (Stage 2, Foreman-ready â€” 10 waves)**\n- Gate command `python -m pytest -v`; each wave ends GREEN. Waves: 1 ConPTY spike (gates whole build) â†’ 2 session registry + worktrees â†’ 3 terminal manager + transport + auth â†’ 4 window-manager UI â†’ 5 thin rows + project summary â†’ 6 in-place session summaries â†’ 7 stage handoffs â†’ 8 runnable deliverable preview â†’ 9 Ghost World Labs branding â†’ 10 CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro-scan/docs.\n- Binding constraints: **no live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the test gate** (stubbed via `tests/fake_claude.py` + `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); `pywinpty` is the only permitted native dep, imported lazily, isolated to the terminal subsystem; f-string brace discipline; token-auth on all mutating/terminal/preview/worktree endpoints; mirror data functions into `anchor.py`.\n- Out of scope (Grass Catchers): multi-tenant terminal server, cross-machine `.anchor`/worktree sync, auto-merging worktree results without review.\n\n**Execution outcome (per the Execution Log)**\n- Crucible Stages 0/1/2 all complete and approved 2026-06-11; Wave 9 (GWL branding) was a mid-Stage-2 addition.\n- **Wave 1 hard gate PASSED:** `spike_conpty_service.py` proved a real pywinpty ConPTY child executing a computed command (not just echo) under a simulated non-interactive service env, and a real `claude` TUI rendered with Max-subscription creds â€” **HALT condition not triggered**. Gate at Wave 1 was 409 passed / 1 skipped; two adversarial reviewers gave GO-WITH-NITS.\n\n*(Per the project memory, all 10 waves later went GREEN â€” 529 passed â€” built by Foreman on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v3`, not yet merged to master.)*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":56831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1800},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8a086ba-f793-4585-9aab-75cfcc33428a","uuid":"98c80d4c-3aff-463a-a857-264de22430a8","request_id":"req_011CbyGtDyE3kR18GkwFeTBE"}
